  "modules.geolinguistics.on_first_use_click_download_dataset_the_map_appears": "On first use, click Download dataset. The map appears after downloading and verification; later visits reuse local data. Alternatively, select an existing geolinguistics-data folder via Select data folder. Data is stored locally in the current account workspace and remains available after reopening. Windows portable builds also read a data folder beside the EXE automatically. macOS and the web use the same folder, with maps and editing processed locally.",
  "modules.geolinguistics.dialect_distribution_browse_county_level_data_compiled_by_jing": "Dialect distribution: browse county-level data compiled by Jing Shaozi. Select original worksheets and filter by province/city/county or macroregion, region, subgroup, and sub-subgroup. Counts use complete parent paths; expand the actual counting list to inspect it.",
  "modules.geolinguistics.dialect_similarity_view_the_paper_s_existing_mds_clustering": "Dialect similarity: view the paper's existing MDS, clustering, and distance results. Selecting a site shows nearby sites; Compare opens item-by-item records for two sites. Filter same/different/missing records by phonetics, lexicon, or grammar, and export the comparison.",
  "modules.geolinguistics.linguistic_phenomena_by_default_broad_categories_show_phenomena_with": "Linguistic phenomena: by default, broad categories show phenomena with verified meanings; the right panel reports coverage for each map. Broad categories aggregate explicitly matched codes, counting a site once per category even if several codes map to it. Sites spanning categories count in each. Fine categories show available specific meanings and retain codes for unverified parts. Filter sites through the legend, favourite maps, and compare two or four maps. All features · Explore codes shows all 510 records. Unverified meanings retain their codes; source details include original map numbers and PDF pages.",
  "modules.geolinguistics.map_wheel_to_zoom_shift_drag_for_box_selection": "Map: wheel to zoom, Shift-drag for box selection. Province/city/county selection filters data; normal panning and zooming change the view only. Enable Current view to make the table follow map bounds.",
  "modules.geolinguistics.my_research_map_add_sites_ipa_and_notes_draw": "My research map: add sites, IPA, and notes; draw areas and annotation lines; import site tables. Edits save locally automatically. Ctrl+S retries saving and Ctrl+Z undoes. Exported projects retain personal edits; PNG, SVG, and tables provide research outputs.",
